    "body": "Right, apart from Safari everyone passes the first test:\r\n```js\r\nfunction assert_transfer_error(transferList) {\r\n  assert_throws(\"DATA_CLONE_ERR\", () => self.postMessage({ get whatever() { throw 1 } }, \"*\", transferList));\r\n}\r\n\r\ntest(() => {\r\n  const b = new ArrayBuffer(1);\r\n  assert_transfer_error([b, b]);\r\n}, \"Cannot transfer the same object twice\");\r\n```\r\nThe later tests are more of a mess, but don't concern this PR (my tentative judgment for those is that we should keep the specification as-is and I filed bugs accordingly).",
